From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:26:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 129/148] fix(ci): name the gascity source from the installed
 gc's vcs.revision (gcp-fooz4)

Upstream's #476 checks out the gascity source at the same commit the gc
binary was built from. The restacked installer instead exported the ref
it was given: `edge` was resolved once for the archive and again by the
checkout's fetch, and edge rotates several times a day (gcp-kinb), so
the two could name different builds. The go-install fallback exported
its REF literally (`latest`, a short sha), which a shallow
`git fetch --depth 1` cannot resolve.

GASCITY_SOURCE_REF is now read from the installed binary with
`go version -m`: the full vcs.revision a release archive's gc records.
When that is absent, the resolved release tag stands in, with a warning.
With neither, the install fails and exports nothing. A `go install
pkg@ref` build is module mode and records no vcs.revision, so the
go-install fallback now always takes that failure branch.

The checkout steps fetch that full SHA and log the full HEAD. The
installer tests add a `go` stub that reads build info out of the fake
gc, so each build carries its own revision. They cover a revision
present (including after an edge rotation and on a cache hit), an
absent revision with a tag fallback, and an absent revision with no
tag (fail).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
